","maxclass":"newobj","text":"live.miditool.out","rect":[65,587,98,23],"patchingRect":[65,587,98,23],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0},{"id":"obj-1","maxclass":"newobj","text":"live.miditool.in","rect":[65,315,203,23],"patchingRect":[65,315,203,23],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":3},{"id":"obj-7","maxclass":"comment","text":"Here we unpack the grid key from the context.\n\nIf the grid is enabled we use the grid resolution (in beats), or fall back to quarter notes.","rect":[451,361,256,94],"patchingRect":[451,361,256,94],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13,"linecount":6},{"id":"obj-5","maxclass":"comment","text":"The live.miditool.in object provides a \"context\" dictionary that contains useful information for building your own MIDI Tools.","rect":[9,84,722,22],"patchingRect":[9,84,722,22],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Lato"},{"id":"obj-6","maxclass":"comment","text":"Note Context","rect":[9,64,153,22],"patchingRect":[9,64,153,22],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Lato","fontsize":13},{"id":"obj-3","maxclass":"comment","text":"live.miditool.in only functions when used inside of a Max for Live Generator or Transformation. You will need to copy the Max patch code into a Transformation or Generator device in Live.","rect":[10,110,556,33],"patchingRect":[10,110,556,33],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial Bold","fontsize":12,"linecount":2},{"id":"obj-4","maxclass":"comment","text":"We can use the grid information from the context outlet also. In this example, we can randomly offset notes within the current grid interval.\n\nThere is also an intensity control which determines how far within the grid interval a note could possibly shift.","rect":[168,170,433,79],"patchingRect":[168,170,433,79],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13,"linecount":5}],"lines":[{"id":"pline-0","sourceId":"obj-1","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-26","targetInlet":0},{"id":"pline-1","sourceId":"obj-1","sourceOutlet":1,"targetId":