,"maxclass":"comment","text":"The data live.miditool.in outputs is in part dependent on a behaviour known as the \"apply cycle\".","rect":[9.5,84,722,22],"patchingRect":[9.5,84,722,22],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Lato"},{"id":"obj-13","maxclass":"comment","text":"Apply Cycle","rect":[9.5,64,153,22],"patchingRect":[9.5,64,153,22],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Lato","fontsize":13},{"id":"obj-12","maxclass":"newobj","text":"dict.pack notes:","rect":[49,531,99,23],"patchingRect":[49,531,99,23],"numinlets":2,"numoutlets":1},{"id":"obj-10","maxclass":"newobj","text":"dict.unpack notes:","rect":[49,435,113,23],"patchingRect":[49,435,113,23],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":2},{"id":"obj-7","maxclass":"comment","text":"live.miditool.in only functions when used inside of a Max for Live Generator or Transformation. You will need to copy the Max patch code into a Transformation or Generator device in Live.","rect":[10,110,556,33],"patchingRect":[10,110,556,33],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial Bold","fontsize":12,"linecount":2},{"id":"obj-19","maxclass":"newobj","text":"p PitchShift","rect":[49,483,74,23],"patchingRect":[49,483,74,23],"numinlets":2,"numoutlets":1},{"id":"obj-8","maxclass":"newobj","text":"t b i","rect":[49,339,29.5,23],"patchingRect":[49,339,29.5,23],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":2},{"id":"obj-6","maxclass":"live.dial","text":"","rect":[49,273,60,54],"patchingRect":[49,273,60,54],"varname":"live.dial","numinlets":1,"numoutlets":2,"parameterEnable":1,"liveParameterEnum":["0","1"],"liveParameterType":1,"liveParameterMmin":-12,"liveParameterMmax":12},{"id":"obj-4","maxclass":"comment","text":"The apply cycle is an important workflow to understand for MIDI Tool generators and transformations.\n\nWhen you send a bang to the live.miditool.in object it triggers the beginning of an \"apply cycle\" which always starts by taking a snapshot of the MIDI editor's content in Live at that time. This snapshot is represented as a dictionary and is output from the object's left outlet. This is a useful behavior to have, because it allows you to structure a MIDI tool so that parameters only affect a given point in time, instead of  constantly modifying the MIDI notes in the clip.\n\nLet us take the example of a pitch shifter MIDI Tool we'd like to make, which has a \"Shift Amount\" parameter. This parameter determines in semitones how far you would like to shift the pitch. If you change this parameter, you don't want to take a new snapshot of the MIDI notes each time you adjust the shift amount. You are more likely to want to experiment with the shift amount, and dial in the amount you would like based on when you first began tweaking the parameter.\n\nAn apply cycle ends when you perform a user interaction with another part of Live such as the browser, transport, session view, etc. or if you perform a user interaction within the MIDI editor itself, such as selecting new notes, adjusting a loop length.\n\nIn other words, the dictionary that you receive from live.miditool.in is always frozen in time at the point at which you started an apply cycle and these cycles can be started and continued by sending a bang to live.miditool.in. If you are already in an apply cycle, the next bang will cause the object to output the same data it snapshotted the first time. If you adjust a parameter then send a bang to live.miditool.in it means that you can adjust the parameter without constantly overwriting the MIDI editor with some new data.\n\nThe last point to remember is that pressing the apply button in Live causes a new apply cycle to begin and end in one interaction.","rect":[292,178,529,486],"patchingRect":[292,178,529,486],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13,"linecount":32},{"id":"obj-11","maxclass":"newobj","text":"live.miditool.out","rect":[49,573,98,23],"patchingRect":[49,573,98,23],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0},{"id":"obj-1","maxclass":"newobj","text":"live.miditool.in","rect":[49,389,90,23],"patchingRect":[49,389,90,23],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":3},{"id":"obj-3","maxclass":"comment","text":"Change this amount and see the results in the MIDI editor.","rect":[103,273,155,54],"patchingRect":[103,273,155,54],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13,"linecount":3,"bubble":1},{"id":"obj-9","maxclass":"textbutton","text":"1","rect":[260,290,20,20],"patchingRect":[260,290,20,20],"ignoreclick":1,"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":3,"fontname":"Arial Bold","textcolor":[0.34902,0.34902,0.34902,1],"bgcolor":[0.9,0.65,0.05,1],"parameterEnable":0}],"lines":[{"id":"pline-0","sourceId":"obj-1","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-10","targetInlet":0},{"id":"pline-1","sourceId":"obj-10","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-19","targetInlet":0},{"id":"pline-2","sourceId":"obj-12","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-11","targetInlet":0},{"id":"pline-3","sourceId":"obj-19","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-12","targetInlet":0},{"id":"pline-4","sourceId":"obj-6","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-8","targetInlet":0},{"id":"pline-5","sourceId":"obj-8","sourceOutlet":0,"targetId":"obj-1","targetInlet":0},{"id":"pline-6","sourceId":"obj-8","sourceOutlet":1,"targetId":"obj-19","targetInlet":1,"midpoints":[69,375,36,375,36,468,113.5,468]}],"helpdetailsHeaderHints":{"sourceBoxId":"obj-2","objectNameHint":"live.miditool.in","headerHeightPx":52,"headerRect":[10,10,315,52]},"stats":{"boxCount":13,"lineCount":7,"presentationBoxCount":0}},"generator":{"pageName":"generator","pageId":"generator__obj-3","renderMode":"page-subpatcher","patcherRect":[0,26,924,796],"boxes":[{"id":"obj-6","maxclass":"comment","text":"Change the number of notes that are generated.","rect":[148.66666666666669,175,139,54],"patchingRect":[148.66666666666669,175,139,54],"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":0,"fontname":"Arial","fontsize":13,"linecount":3,"bubble":1},{"id":"obj-9","maxclass":"textbutton","text":"1","rect":[295,192,20,20],"patchingRect":[295,192,20,20],"ignoreclick":1,"numinlets":1,"numoutlets":3,"fontna